# Rescue Girl, First Responder: "{T}: Return another target permanent you control to its owner's hand. Activate only during
# your turn." On turn 3 (no longer summoning sick) she cannot target herself ("another", refused). On Bot2's turn 4, untapped
# and able to tap, she still cannot be activated (CR 602.5b: only during your turn). On turn 5 she returns Bot1's Island.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Rescue Girl, First Responder
Island
Island
Island
Island
Island
Island x30

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x30

[Actions]
[Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: White)
Bot1.Hand.Rescue Girl, First Responder.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
! Bot1.Battlefield.Rescue Girl, First Responder.Activate(Bot1.Battlefield.Rescue Girl, First Responder)
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Rescue Girl, First Responder.Tapped = false
! Bot1.Battlefield.Rescue Girl, First Responder.Activate(Bot1.Battlefield.Island)
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Rescue Girl, First Responder.Activate(Bot1.Battlefield.Island)
[Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Rescue Girl, First Responder
Bot1.Battlefield.Rescue Girl, First Responder.Tapped = true
